// The monitor followed: the kernel's picture brought to the output of a
// Polaris card (DCE 11.2) where the monitor is, at boot and while brixOS
// runs. gpu_plug.mlx says where something is plugged in and what its
// EDID says; gpu_mode.mlx's `makeTo` plans the picture's way to another
// output (or the same output's mode set again), gpu_set.mlx carries the
// plan out with every write read back, every table's answer checked and
// a way back. This file is the rule between them, and it says in the log
// every time it decides.
//
// THE RULE (the study's 5.6, gpu-autoswitch.verified.md; every rule is
// ours, Linux leaves all of it to programs). One picture, one controller:
// the one that runs is the one that stays (3.3), only its way out
// changes.
// - A: the output that shows the picture has nothing plugged in for
//   certain (its hot plug line low) and another connector has a monitor
//   whose EDID was read and holds: the picture is brought there. At boot
//   at once; while brixOS runs only after the showing output's line has
//   been low for a second (HOLD): a monitor that sleeps with its line low
//   and a second one plugged in elsewhere look the same for a moment.
//   Several such connectors: an HDMI one first, then DVI, then a
//   DisplayPort one that sends TMDS, then DisplayPort; among equals the
//   ROM's order ("HDMI first where an order is needed", the user's word).
// - B: a second monitor while the first shows the picture: the picture
//   stays where it is; the second is said and not driven.
// - C: the showing output's monitor gone and none elsewhere: nothing is
//   taken down (the controller and the transmitter keep running into the
//   empty connector, as under Linux until a program acts); said once.
// - The showing output's monitor back (switched off and on, or to another
//   input and back, with its line low meanwhile): its EDID is read again.
//   The same EDID: the output is checked (its back end still sends the
//   controller that runs) and nothing is written; the log says how long
//   the line was low. (With no EDID known from before, as after a boot
//   with nothing plugged in, the monitor counts as another one: D.)
//   Below 340 MHz an HDMI or DVI monitor keeps nothing
//   of the source while it is off (no SCDC is told here: the study's 5.3,
//   corrected: Linux writes the SCDC bytes at every enable; this driver
//   plans no clock that needs them). If the output does not send any more
//   (this driver never takes it down; something else would have), its
//   mode set again on the same output is tried: a plan starts from the
//   output that runs, so with its back end off it is refused and the
//   reason said. A monitor whose line never moves is not seen and needs
//   nothing.
// - D: a monitor of another size than the picture: the picture keeps its
//   size (programs draw on it); the same size (the same monitor moved, the
//   usual case) is followed, another is said, not followed, and a restart
//   gives the monitor its own mode. (The study's 6.5 stage 4 has "D 1
//   only"; a listed timing of the picture's size, a picture in the middle
//   with borders and a cut picture are its stage 6, not built.)
// - E: something plugged in that gives no EDID (after the plug item's
//   second asking): not driven, said.
// - F: the showing output's line cannot be judged: its monitor counts as
//   there. Only at boot, when nothing answers on its DDC line and a
//   monitor elsewhere answers, the picture is brought there; while brixOS
//   runs nothing is moved away from such an output.
// - A DisplayPort connector, as either end of a move: followed as an HDMI
//   or DVI one is, by what its monitor said over its AUX channel
//   (gpu_dpwatch.mlx asks it when its line comes high: the rule waits for
//   that as for an EDID being read over DDC): a monitor that answers with
//   an EDID that holds and is one a link is trained to is a monitor here;
//   one that does not answer gives no EDID (E); one no link is trained to
//   (an adapter or a hub, a revision before 1.1) is said and not driven.
//   The move is gpu_mode.mlx's "A MOVE WITH A DISPLAYPORT END", carried
//   out with the AUX channels of both DisplayPort ends lent. A connector
//   of a kind no path of this driver's leaves by is said and not driven.
// - The firmware started no output of this card: nothing is brought up.
//   That needs a controller started from nothing (the study's 4.4), whose
//   format words come from a controller that runs; with none running not
//   every word is known.
// - The choice: only a boot that lets the driver write the display and
//   sets the monitor's own mode follows ("native"). "Firmware" asks
//   nobody and writes nothing; "ask" and "rehearsal" ask, and the
//   monitor is not followed: the log says what would be done (`How`).
// - The keys at boot never name an output.
//
// WHILE brixOS RUNS (`tick`, from the timer's tick on the first processor,
// after gpu_plug.mlx's look): the decision is a few reads of the record,
// made in the timer's interrupt; a change it decides is given back and
// carried out (`carry`) once the interrupt is over, on the trap's way
// back (gpu_together.mlx's `carryDue`, which also keeps it off a mode a
// program asked for), with the kernel's lock held all along and every
// other processor held still while the card is written (gpu_change.mlx's
// `held`, the mode change's machinery). Programs draw into the picture's
// memory, which a move does not touch (same place, size and pitch:
// nothing is told to any program, takePicture is not called), and the
// console is drawn on that same memory or not at all (gpu.mlx keeps it
// for the log alone while the screen is dark). Nothing else writes a
// register of the display; the I2C engine is the plug item's and no
// reading may run meanwhile, so a move waits until none does. How long
// the screen is dark at most is said before the first write
// (gpu_set.mlx's `longest`: the plan's own bounds, a table two seconds, a
// state a tenth); the card's log of 17 Nov has a mode set's parts at
// about a second. The card is read out again first (the frames counted)
// only when something wrote it since the last read-out.
// A move that fails goes back by gpu_set.mlx's way back to the output the
// picture was on (its four endings hold); when its monitor has left, the
// log says that no monitor shows the picture now. It is tried again when
// a line or an EDID changes, else after 5 and 30 seconds, three times in
// all (the study's 6.4); then it is left, said. A way back that did not
// end in the state of before ends the following at this boot, said (the
// study's 6.4 would run that way back once more from where the card is:
// not built).
const scanout = @import("./gpu_display.mlx")
const mode = @import("./gpu_mode.mlx")
const modeset = @import("./gpu_set.mlx")
const videorom = @import("./gpu_rom.mlx")
const edid = @import("./edid.mlx")
const ddc = @import("./gpu_ddc.mlx")
const plug = @import("./gpu_plug.mlx")
const changing = @import("./gpu_change.mlx")
const dplink = @import("./gpu_link.mlx")
const aux = @import("./gpu_aux.mlx")
const dpwatch = @import("./gpu_dpwatch.mlx")

pub const NONE: usize = plug.NONE
// Ours, in nanoseconds: how long the showing output's line is low before
// the picture leaves it while brixOS runs; when a move that failed is
// tried again, and how often in all.
pub const HOLD: usize = 1000000000
pub const AGAIN = [_]usize{ 5000000000, 30000000000 }
pub const TRIES: usize = 3
pub const BACK_ENDS: usize = 7

// How far this boot's choice lets the rule go.
pub const How = enum(u8) {
    // There is nothing to follow: no card whose connectors are known (or
    // no more at this boot: a way back that did not end in the state of
    // before, `carried`).
    off,
    // "firmware": nobody is asked and nothing written; said what would be.
    quiet,
    // "ask", "rehearsal": monitors are asked, not followed; said likewise.
    says,
    // The default: the monitor is followed.
    follows
}

// What the rule decided.
pub const Act = enum(u8) {
    // Nothing to do: the picture is where the monitor is, or nothing
    // better is known.
    stay,
    // The picture brought to another output (A).
    move,
    // A move that waits: the hold, an EDID still being read.
    wait,
    // The showing output's monitor gone, none elsewhere: kept (C).
    kept,
    // A second monitor while the first shows the picture (B).
    second,
    // The showing output's monitor back, the same one, the output sending.
    back,
    // The same, and the output does not send any more: its mode set again.
    again,
    // Another monitor on the showing output, of the picture's size: its
    // mode set.
    other,
    // A monitor of another size than the picture (D): not followed.
    size,
    // Something plugged in that gives no EDID (E).
    unanswered,
    // A monitor on a DisplayPort connector that no link is trained to, or
    // something on a connector of a kind no path leaves by: not driven.
    displayport,
    // The firmware started no output of this card.
    none_started,
    // A move tried TRIES times: left.
    given_up
}

pub const Decision = struct {
    act: Act
    // The connector the decision is about, and the one that shows the
    // picture (NONE: none).
    to: usize
    from: usize
}

// The record of the card for the rule (the study's 6.2, "one record for
// the card").
pub const Follow = struct {
    how: How
    // The connector that shows the picture (NONE: none of the ROM's, or
    // several), its controller, and the picture's size.
    showing: usize
    controller: usize
    width: usize
    height: usize
    // The EDID of the monitor the picture was last set for (or found
    // with at boot), and the timing it is sent (the clock this driver
    // set, 0: the firmware's; its totals); the whole timing when this
    // driver set it (`timed`: at boot, by a move, or by a mode a program
    // asked for, gpu_together.mlx).
    edid: [ddc.ROOM]u8
    edidCount: usize
    clock: usize
    hTotal: usize
    vTotal: usize
    timing: edid.Timing
    timed: bool
    // The showing output's line: since when it is low (from the plug
    // item's record); its monitor's return is being asked for; how long
    // its line was low then.
    lowAt: usize
    returning: bool
    lowFor: usize
    // Per connector: the reading of its EDID last seen (the plug item's
    // `heardAt`), and what was said of it last (to say it once).
    heardAt: [videorom.CONNECTORS]usize
    said: [videorom.CONNECTORS]Act
    keptSaid: bool
    // Per back end: its transmitter was made ready at this boot (the
    // firmware's own, or this driver's "init").
    ready: [BACK_ENDS]bool
    // A move that did not come about: how often it was tried, when once
    // more.
    tries: usize
    retryAt: usize
    // Moves and mode sets carried out at this boot.
    moves: usize
}

// What a change is carried out with (gpu.mlx's, or a test's): the card's
// hands and tables, the ROM's facts, the read-out, the kernel's picture,
// room for the plan and what became of it; and the mode change's
// machinery (gpu_change.mlx's `held`: every other processor held still
// while the card is written) with its record (how long they stood still;
// whether the read-out is the card's as it is now). In the kernel the
// read-out, the picture, the plan and the result are that record's own
// (gpu_together.mlx): one record of the card's display for both.
pub const Lent = struct {
    hands: *const modeset.Hands
    tables: ?*const modeset.Tables
    rom: *const mode.Rom
    memory: *const scanout.Memory
    readout: *scanout.Readout
    plan: *mode.Plan
    result: *modeset.Result
    change: *const changing.Lent
    seen: *changing.Seen
}

fn silent(text: []const u8) -> void {}

// The monitors on DisplayPort connectors and their AUX channels
// (gpu_dpwatch.mlx; gpu.mlx lends them): what a move with a DisplayPort
// end is carried out with. None: such a move is not carried out.
var sinks: ?*dpwatch.Sinks = null // (per run)

pub fn useSinks(s: ?*dpwatch.Sinks) -> void { sinks = s }

// Whether a connector is a DisplayPort one whose monitor is asked over the
// AUX channel (not one that sends TMDS through an adapter).
fn dpPort(port: *const plug.Port) -> bool { return port.*.rom.kind == videorom.CONNECTOR_OBJECT_ID_DISPLAYPORT && !(port.*.firmware && port.*.sends == plug.Sends.tmds) }

// Whether a DisplayPort connector's monitor answered on its AUX channel
// and is one a link is trained to.
fn trainable(port: *const plug.Port) -> bool { return port.*.dp.state == dplink.Asked.heard && port.*.dp.refusal == dplink.Refusal.none }

// The record begun once the boot's own change is over (`atBoot` was
// first): what serves the connectors now, the picture's size, the EDID
// it was set for and the timing it is sent (`clock` 0: the firmware's).
// What was said at boot stays said; `carried` adds what the boot's own
// plan did.
pub fn begin(follow: *Follow, how: How, ports: *const plug.Ports, controller: usize, width: usize, height: usize, bytes: []const u8, clock: usize, hTotal: usize, vTotal: usize) -> void {
    follow.*.how = if ports.*.found { how } else { How.off }
    follow.*.controller = controller
    follow.*.showing = only(ports, controller)
    follow.*.width = width
    follow.*.height = height
    keepEdid(follow, bytes)
    follow.*.clock = clock
    follow.*.hTotal = hTotal
    follow.*.vTotal = vTotal
    follow.*.timed = false
    follow.*.lowAt = 0
    follow.*.returning = false
    follow.*.lowFor = 0
    follow.*.keptSaid = false
    follow.*.tries = 0
    follow.*.retryAt = 0
    var k: usize = 0
    while k < videorom.CONNECTORS {
        follow.*.heardAt[k] = 0
        if k < ports.*.count {
            const port = &ports.*.ports[k]
            follow.*.heardAt[k] = port.*.heardAt
            if port.*.firmware && port.*.rom.transmitter < BACK_ENDS { follow.*.ready[port.*.rom.transmitter] = true }
            if k == follow.*.showing && port.*.level == plug.Level.low { follow.*.lowAt = port.*.since }
        }
        k += 1
    }
}

// The connector `controller`'s picture goes out by when it is exactly
// one; NONE otherwise.
fn only(ports: *const plug.Ports, controller: usize) -> usize {
    var found: usize = NONE
    var k: usize = 0
    while k < ports.*.count {
        const port = &ports.*.ports[k]
        if port.*.firmware && port.*.controller == controller {
            if found != NONE { return NONE }
            found = k
        }
        k += 1
    }
    return found
}

fn keepEdid(follow: *Follow, bytes: []const u8) -> void {
    const count = if bytes.length > ddc.ROOM { ddc.ROOM } else { bytes.length }
    var k: usize = 0
    while k < count {
        follow.*.edid[k] = bytes[k]
        k += 1
    }
    follow.*.edidCount = count
}

// Which comes first when several connectors have a monitor: HDMI, DVI, a
// DisplayPort connector that sends TMDS, DisplayPort (and anything else
// last).
fn rank(port: *const plug.Port) -> usize {
    const kind = port.*.rom.kind
    if kind == videorom.CONNECTOR_OBJECT_ID_HDMI_TYPE_A || kind == videorom.CONNECTOR_OBJECT_ID_HDMI_TYPE_B { return 0 }
    if port.tmdsKind() { return 1 }
    if kind == videorom.CONNECTOR_OBJECT_ID_DISPLAYPORT { return if port.*.sends == plug.Sends.tmds { 2 } else { 3 } }
    return 4
}

// Whether a connector's monitor answered with an EDID that holds and
// names a timing of its own.
fn heard(port: *const plug.Port) -> bool { return port.*.heard.outcome == ddc.Outcome.read && port.*.monitor.state == edid.State.found }

// Whether a connector's monitor is the one the picture was last set for:
// its EDID the record's, as far as both go.
fn same(port: *const plug.Port, follow: *const Follow) -> bool {
    if !heard(port) { return false }
    var at: usize = 0
    return plug.against(&port.*.heard, follow.*.edid[0..follow.*.edidCount], &at) == plug.Against.same
}

// Whether the picture as it is can be given to a connector's monitor: its
// own size is the picture's (its own timing is set), or it is the monitor
// the picture was last set for and this driver set the timing that runs
// (after a mode a program asked for that is a size of the person's
// choosing: the monitor showed it a moment ago, and gets it again).
fn fits(port: *const plug.Port, follow: *const Follow) -> bool {
    if port.*.monitor.width == follow.*.width && port.*.monitor.height == follow.*.height { return true }
    return follow.*.timed && follow.*.timing.width == follow.*.width && follow.*.timing.height == follow.*.height && same(port, follow)
}

// The monitor a change's plan is made for: the connector's own; for the
// monitor the picture was last set for, while it is sent a timing this
// driver set other than its own, that timing as its own (as gpu_change.mlx
// plans a mode a program asked for), with what its EDID says of HDMI.
fn planned(port: *const plug.Port, follow: *const Follow, monitor: *edid.Monitor, offer: *edid.Offer) -> void {
    monitor.* = port.*.monitor
    offer.* = port.*.offer
    if !follow.*.timed || !same(port, follow) { return }
    const t = &follow.*.timing
    const own = &port.*.monitor.timing
    if t.*.clock == own.*.clock && t.*.width == own.*.width && t.*.height == own.*.height && t.*.hTotal == own.*.hTotal && t.*.vTotal == own.*.vTotal { return }
    monitor.* = changing.asMonitor(t)
    offer.*.count = 0
}

// Whether its monitor is still to be asked, or being asked.
fn asking(port: *const plug.Port, reading: usize) -> bool { return port.*.askAt != 0 || reading == port.*.index }

// The connector the picture would be brought to: the first, in the order
// of `rank` and then the ROM's, with its line high and a monitor that
// answered (`quiet`: whose line is high: nobody is asked). The first
// connector met that has to be said instead (a DisplayPort one, one
// that gives no EDID, one whose monitor has another size) is the
// decision when no connector is found; a monitor still being asked makes
// it a wait.
fn choose(ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *const Follow, reading: usize, quiet: bool) -> Decision {
    var said = Decision.{ .act = Act.stay, .to = NONE, .from = follow.*.showing }
    var r: usize = 0
    while r < 5 {
        var k: usize = 0
        while k < ports.*.count {
            const port = &ports.*.ports[k]
            k += 1
            if port.*.index == follow.*.showing || port.*.level != plug.Level.high || rank(port) != r { continue }
            if r >= 4 {
                if said.act == Act.stay { said = Decision.{ .act = Act.displayport, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
                continue
            }
            if quiet { return Decision.{ .act = Act.move, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
            if asking(port, reading) { return Decision.{ .act = Act.wait, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
            if !heard(port) {
                if said.act == Act.stay { said = Decision.{ .act = Act.unanswered, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
                continue
            }
            if dpPort(port) && !trainable(port) {
                if said.act == Act.stay { said = Decision.{ .act = Act.displayport, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
                continue
            }
            // (What a boot that follows the monitor would do is said
            // whatever the size: that boot gives the picture its size.)
            if follow.*.how == How.follows && !fits(port, follow) {
                if said.act == Act.stay { said = Decision.{ .act = Act.size, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
                continue
            }
            return Decision.{ .act = Act.move, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing }
        }
        r += 1
    }
    return said
}

// The first connector besides the showing one with a monitor that has
// not been said yet (B, or E or a DisplayPort one), as a decision; stay
// when there is none.
fn others(ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *const Follow, reading: usize, quiet: bool) -> Decision {
    var k: usize = 0
    while k < ports.*.count {
        const port = &ports.*.ports[k]
        k += 1
        if port.*.index == follow.*.showing || port.*.level != plug.Level.high { continue }
        var act = Act.second
        if rank(port) >= 4 {
            act = Act.displayport
        } else if !quiet && asking(port, reading) {
            continue
        } else if !quiet && !heard(port) {
            act = Act.unanswered
        } else if !quiet && dpPort(port) && !trainable(port) {
            act = Act.displayport
        }
        if follow.*.said[port.*.index] != act { return Decision.{ .act = act, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
    }
    return Decision.{ .act = Act.stay, .to = NONE, .from = follow.*.showing }
}

// The rule at boot (the file's head): where the monitor is against where
// the firmware's picture goes out, from the plug item's survey, the
// EDIDs read at boot and what it detected; said. A move is carried out by
// gpu.mlx's plan for this boot (its picture takes the monitor's own size
// there, no program runs yet).
pub fn atBoot(card: *const scanout.Card, ports: *const plug.Ports, verdict: *const plug.Verdict, follow: *Follow, how: How) -> Decision {
    follow.*.how = if ports.*.found { how } else { How.off }
    follow.*.showing = if verdict.*.outputs == 1 { verdict.*.output } else { NONE }
    follow.*.width = 0
    follow.*.height = 0
    follow.*.clock = 0
    follow.*.tries = 0
    follow.*.retryAt = 0
    follow.*.moves = 0
    var n: usize = 0
    while n < BACK_ENDS {
        follow.*.ready[n] = false
        n += 1
    }
    var k: usize = 0
    while k < videorom.CONNECTORS {
        follow.*.said[k] = Act.stay
        // (A transmitter the firmware runs was made ready by it.)
        if k < ports.*.count && ports.*.ports[k].firmware && ports.*.ports[k].rom.transmitter < BACK_ENDS { follow.*.ready[ports.*.ports[k].rom.transmitter] = true }
        k += 1
    }
    var d = Decision.{ .act = Act.stay, .to = NONE, .from = follow.*.showing }
    if follow.*.how == How.off { return d }
    const quiet = how == How.quiet
    if verdict.*.what == plug.Case.not_started {
        d.act = Act.none_started
        d.to = verdict.*.other
        sayBoot(card, ports, follow, d)
        return d
    }
    if follow.*.showing == NONE { return d }
    const showing = &ports.*.ports[follow.*.showing]
    // F: a line that cannot be judged, and nothing answers on its DDC
    // line.
    const away = showing.*.level == plug.Level.low || (!showing.judged() && showing.*.heard.outcome == ddc.Outcome.no_answer)
    if away { d = chooseAtBoot(ports, follow, quiet) }
    if d.act == Act.move {
        sayBoot(card, ports, follow, d)
        follow.*.said[d.to] = Act.move
        return d
    }
    if d.act == Act.displayport || d.act == Act.unanswered {
        sayOther(card, ports, follow, d)
        follow.*.said[d.to] = d.act
    }
    d = Decision.{ .act = Act.stay, .to = NONE, .from = follow.*.showing }
    sayBoot(card, ports, follow, d)
    // The others, each said once.
    var o = others(ports, follow, NONE, quiet)
    while o.act != Act.stay {
        sayOther(card, ports, follow, o)
        follow.*.said[o.to] = o.act
        o = others(ports, follow, NONE, quiet)
    }
    return d
}

// `choose` at boot, where any size goes: the monitor's own size is what
// the boot's picture takes.
fn chooseAtBoot(ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *Follow, quiet: bool) -> Decision {
    var r: usize = 0
    var said = Decision.{ .act = Act.stay, .to = NONE, .from = follow.*.showing }
    while r < 5 {
        var k: usize = 0
        while k < ports.*.count {
            const port = &ports.*.ports[k]
            k += 1
            if port.*.index == follow.*.showing || port.*.level != plug.Level.high || rank(port) != r { continue }
            if r >= 4 {
                if said.act == Act.stay { said = Decision.{ .act = Act.displayport, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
                continue
            }
            if quiet || (heard(port) && (!dpPort(port) || trainable(port))) { return Decision.{ .act = Act.move, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
            if said.act == Act.stay { said = Decision.{ .act = if heard(port) { Act.displayport } else { Act.unanswered }, .to = port.*.index, .from = follow.*.showing } }
        }
        r += 1
    }
    return said
}

// The plan's target for a decision: the connector, whether its
// transmitter is still to be made ready, whether the picture stays as it
// is (while brixOS runs it does), the clock this driver last set.
pub fn targetFor(ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *const Follow, d: Decision, keep: bool) -> mode.Target {
    const port = &ports.*.ports[d.to]
    const back = port.*.rom.transmitter
    const ready = back < BACK_ENDS && follow.*.ready[back]
    return mode.Target.{ .index = d.to, .connector = port.*.rom, .from = follow.*.showing, .init = !ready, .keep = keep, .clock = follow.*.clock }
}

// What a carried out plan leaves in the record (at boot too): the
// transmitter made ready when the plan went past its "init", the
// picture's way out and what it is sent when it holds. A change the rule
// decided that did not come about counts as a try, said with where the
// picture is now and when it is tried once more. One whose way back did
// not end in the state of before (gpu_set.mlx's "lost" and "astray": the
// output is left as that left it until a restart) is not tried again, and
// from then on the monitor is not followed at this boot: a plan made from
// a state nobody planned could only make it worse.
pub fn carried(card: *const scanout.Card, follow: *Follow, ports: *const plug.Ports, plan: *const mode.Plan, result: *const modeset.Result, d: Decision) -> bool {
    const done = result.*.outcome == modeset.Outcome.done
    if plan.*.move.init && (done || (result.*.outcome != modeset.Outcome.untouched && result.*.step > plan.*.move.initAt)) && plan.*.tmds.backEnd < BACK_ENDS { follow.*.ready[plan.*.tmds.backEnd] = true }
    if !done {
        if follow.*.how != How.follows || (d.act != Act.move && d.act != Act.again && d.act != Act.other) { return false }
        follow.*.tries += 1
        // (Where the picture is now, when the way back took it there.)
        const outcome = result.*.outcome
        if outcome == modeset.Outcome.lost || outcome == modeset.Outcome.astray {
            follow.*.how = How.off
            follow.*.returning = false
            card.say("gpu: the monitor is not followed any more at this boot: the way back did not end in the state of before (a restart starts from the firmware's picture again)\n")
            return false
        }
        if d.act == Act.move && (outcome == modeset.Outcome.back || outcome == modeset.Outcome.unsure) && d.from < ports.*.count {
            card.say("gpu: back on ")
            plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.from])
            card.say(", where no monitor is; the monitor on ")
            plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.to])
            card.say(" is not shown\n")
        }
        if follow.*.tries < TRIES {
            follow.*.retryAt = card.time() + AGAIN[follow.*.tries - 1]
            card.field("gpu: once more in ", AGAIN[follow.*.tries - 1] / 1000000000)
            card.field(" s (try ", follow.*.tries)
            card.field(" of ", TRIES)
            card.say(")\n")
        }
        return false
    }
    follow.*.showing = only(ports, plan.*.controller)
    follow.*.controller = plan.*.controller
    follow.*.width = plan.*.width
    follow.*.height = plan.*.height
    follow.*.clock = plan.*.timing.clock
    follow.*.hTotal = plan.*.timing.hTotal
    follow.*.vTotal = plan.*.timing.vTotal
    follow.*.timing = plan.*.timing
    follow.*.timed = true
    if d.to < ports.*.count { keepEdid(follow, ports.*.ports[d.to].heard.data()) }
    follow.*.lowAt = 0
    follow.*.returning = false
    follow.*.keptSaid = false
    follow.*.tries = 0
    follow.*.moves += 1
    return true
}

// A mode a program asked for, or the mode before it put back, set on the
// output that shows the picture (gpu_together.mlx): from now on the
// record's picture is the plan's, its size, the timing it is sent and the
// clock this driver set, so that the same-size rule and the monitor's
// return are judged by what runs; the output stays. The monitor the
// picture was set for is the one there now: its EDID is the record's when
// it answered (another monitor may have come there without anything set
// for it: one of another size, or one that takes the timing sent). A
// change whose way back did not end in the state of before ends the
// following at this boot, as a move's does (`carried`).
pub fn modeChanged(card: *const scanout.Card, follow: *Follow, ports: *const plug.Ports, plan: *const mode.Plan, result: *const modeset.Result) -> void {
    const outcome = result.*.outcome
    if outcome == modeset.Outcome.done {
        follow.*.controller = plan.*.controller
        const s = only(ports, plan.*.controller)
        if s != NONE { follow.*.showing = s }
        follow.*.width = plan.*.width
        follow.*.height = plan.*.height
        follow.*.clock = plan.*.timing.clock
        follow.*.hTotal = plan.*.timing.hTotal
        follow.*.vTotal = plan.*.timing.vTotal
        follow.*.timing = plan.*.timing
        follow.*.timed = true
        if follow.*.showing < ports.*.count {
            const port = &ports.*.ports[follow.*.showing]
            if port.*.level == plug.Level.high && heard(port) { keepEdid(follow, port.*.heard.data()) }
        }
        return
    }
    if (outcome == modeset.Outcome.lost || outcome == modeset.Outcome.astray) && follow.*.how != How.off {
        follow.*.how = How.off
        follow.*.returning = false
        card.say("gpu: the monitor is not followed any more at this boot: the way back did not end in the state of before (a restart starts from the firmware's picture again)\n")
    }
}

// A line of the plug item's record taken at this look: the showing
// output's monitor gone or back; anything else that changed lets a move
// that failed be tried again, and what was said of the connector be said
// anew.
fn noteChange(follow: *Follow, ports: *const plug.Ports, change: *const plug.Change) -> void {
    follow.*.tries = 0
    follow.*.retryAt = 0
    const port = &ports.*.ports[change.*.port]
    if change.*.port != follow.*.showing {
        follow.*.said[change.*.port] = Act.stay
        return
    }
    if change.*.now == plug.Level.low {
        follow.*.lowAt = port.*.since
        follow.*.returning = false
        follow.*.keptSaid = false
    } else if change.*.now == plug.Level.high && follow.*.lowAt != 0 {
        follow.*.returning = true
        follow.*.lowFor = if port.*.since > follow.*.lowAt { port.*.since - follow.*.lowAt } else { 0 }
        follow.*.lowAt = 0
    }
}

fn less(a: usize, b: usize) -> usize { return if a > b { a - b } else { 0 } }

// The rule while brixOS runs, from the record as it stands (the file's
// head).
pub fn decide(ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *Follow, reading: usize, now: usize) -> Decision {
    var d = Decision.{ .act = Act.stay, .to = NONE, .from = follow.*.showing }
    const s = follow.*.showing
    if s == NONE || s >= ports.*.count { return d }
    const quiet = follow.*.how == How.quiet
    const showing = &ports.*.ports[s]
    if showing.*.level == plug.Level.low {
        d = choose(ports, follow, reading, quiet)
        if d.act == Act.move && less(now, showing.*.since) < HOLD { d.act = Act.wait }
        if d.act == Act.stay { d = Decision.{ .act = Act.kept, .to = s, .from = s } }
        // (What has to be said of another connector is said once.)
        if (d.act == Act.unanswered || d.act == Act.displayport || d.act == Act.size) && follow.*.said[d.to] == d.act { d.act = Act.stay }
        return d
    }
    if showing.*.level == plug.Level.high && follow.*.returning && !quiet {
        if asking(showing, reading) { return Decision.{ .act = Act.wait, .to = s, .from = s } }
        follow.*.returning = false
        d.to = s
        if !heard(showing) {
            d.act = Act.unanswered
            return d
        }
        var at: usize = 0
        const before = follow.*.edid[0..follow.*.edidCount]
        // (The same monitor only when its EDID is the one the picture was
        // set for or found with: with none known from before, as after a
        // boot with nothing plugged in, it counts as another one. A mode
        // set to be tried keeps the return open until it came about or
        // was given up: a try that fails is made once more.)
        if plug.against(&showing.*.heard, before, &at) == plug.Against.same {
            d.act = if showing.*.firmware && showing.*.controller == follow.*.controller { Act.back } else { Act.again }
            follow.*.returning = d.act == Act.again && follow.*.how == How.follows
            return d
        }
        const m = &showing.*.monitor
        if m.*.width != follow.*.width || m.*.height != follow.*.height {
            d.act = Act.size
            return d
        }
        // (Another monitor that takes the timing sent already: nothing
        // to set.)
        const t = &m.*.timing
        const same = follow.*.clock != 0 && less(t.*.clock, follow.*.clock) + less(follow.*.clock, t.*.clock) <= follow.*.clock / 200 && t.*.hTotal == follow.*.hTotal && t.*.vTotal == follow.*.vTotal
        d.act = if same { Act.back } else { Act.other }
        follow.*.returning = d.act == Act.other && follow.*.how == How.follows
        return d
    }
    if showing.*.level == plug.Level.high && follow.*.returning && quiet { follow.*.returning = false }
    return others(ports, follow, reading, quiet)
}

// The rule's turn at a tick of the timer (gpu_together.mlx's `tick`,
// after gpu_plug.mlx's): what changed taken into the record, the rule
// decided and what it decided said. A change this boot carries out (a
// move, a mode set again, another monitor's timing) is not made here, in
// the timer's interrupt: it is given back (stay: none), and `carry` makes
// it once the interrupt is over (gpu_together.mlx's `carryDue`).
pub fn tick(card: *const scanout.Card, follow: *Follow, watch: *plug.Watch) -> Decision {
    const none = Decision.{ .act = Act.stay, .to = NONE, .from = follow.*.showing }
    if follow.*.how == How.off { return none }
    const ports = &watch.*.ports
    var k: usize = 0
    while k < watch.*.changes.count {
        noteChange(follow, ports, &watch.*.changes.list[k])
        k += 1
    }
    k = 0
    while k < ports.*.count {
        if ports.*.ports[k].heardAt != follow.*.heardAt[k] {
            follow.*.heardAt[k] = ports.*.ports[k].heardAt
            follow.*.tries = 0
            follow.*.retryAt = 0
        }
        k += 1
    }
    // (One user of the card's display at a time: no change while an EDID
    // is being read.)
    if watch.*.reading != NONE { return none }
    const now = card.time()
    const d = decide(ports, follow, watch.*.reading, now)
    return act(card, follow, watch, d, now)
}

// What was decided said, once where it is to be said once; the change to
// carry out given back (stay: none).
fn act(card: *const scanout.Card, follow: *Follow, watch: *plug.Watch, d: Decision, now: usize) -> Decision {
    const ports = &watch.*.ports
    const none = Decision.{ .act = Act.stay, .to = NONE, .from = follow.*.showing }
    if d.act == Act.stay || d.act == Act.wait { return none }
    if d.act == Act.kept {
        if follow.*.keptSaid { return none }
        follow.*.keptSaid = true
        sayKept(card, ports, d.from)
        return none
    }
    if d.act == Act.back {
        sayBack(card, ports, follow, d)
        return none
    }
    // (The monitor back on the DisplayPort output that shows the picture,
    // or another one there: its link was looked at as it came (gpu_dpwatch.
    // mlx); setting that output's mode anew is not built, and a TMDS
    // output's plan is none for it. Said once, nothing written.)
    if (d.act == Act.again || d.act == Act.other) && d.to < ports.*.count && dpPort(&ports.*.ports[d.to]) {
        follow.*.returning = false
        sayDpReturn(card, ports, follow, d)
        return none
    }
    if d.act != Act.move && d.act != Act.again && d.act != Act.other {
        if follow.*.said[d.to] == d.act { return none }
        follow.*.said[d.to] = d.act
        sayOther(card, ports, follow, d)
        return none
    }
    if follow.*.how != How.follows {
        if follow.*.said[d.to] == d.act { return none }
        follow.*.said[d.to] = d.act
        sayWould(card, ports, follow, d)
        return none
    }
    if follow.*.tries >= TRIES {
        // (The output's own mode set again is not asked for any more.)
        follow.*.returning = false
        if follow.*.said[d.to] == Act.given_up { return none }
        follow.*.said[d.to] = Act.given_up
        card.say("gpu: ")
        plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.to])
        card.field(if d.act == Act.move { ": the picture was not brought there in " } else { ": the output's mode was not set again in " }, TRIES)
        card.say(" tries: it is left until a line or an EDID changes\n")
        return none
    }
    if now < follow.*.retryAt { return none }
    return d
}

// A change while brixOS runs carried out (the file's head): said before
// the screen goes dark, the card read out again unless the read-out is
// the card's as it is now (quietly: the boot's read-out is in the log),
// the plan made for the decision's connector with the picture kept (for
// the monitor the picture was last set for, the timing it was sent:
// `planned`), said and listed, carried out by the mode change's machinery
// with every other processor held still, and the record brought up to
// date.
pub fn carry(card: *const scanout.Card, lent: *const Lent, follow: *Follow, watch: *plug.Watch, d: Decision) -> bool {
    const ports = &watch.*.ports
    const port = &ports.*.ports[d.to]
    card.say("gpu: ")
    if d.act == Act.move {
        card.say("the monitor is on ")
        plug.sayName(card, port)
        card.say(" now, and nothing is plugged into ")
        plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.from])
        card.say(": the picture is brought there")
    } else if d.act == Act.again {
        plug.sayName(card, port)
        card.say(": the monitor is back, and the output does not send any more: its mode is set again")
    } else {
        plug.sayName(card, port)
        card.say(": another monitor of the picture's size: its own timing is set")
    }
    card.say(" (every other processor stands still while the card is written; the picture's memory stays as it is)\n")
    if !lent.*.seen.*.fresh {
        const quiet = scanout.Card.{ .read = card.*.read, .now = card.*.now, .write = silent }
        scanout.report(&quiet, lent.*.memory, lent.*.readout)
    }
    const target = targetFor(ports, follow, d, true)
    var monitor: edid.Monitor = undefined
    var offer: edid.Offer = undefined
    planned(port, follow, &monitor, &offer)
    // (A DisplayPort end: what its monitor said, and its AUX channel.)
    const from = if d.from < ports.*.count { &ports.*.ports[d.from] } else { port }
    var there: ?*const dplink.Heard = null
    var before: ?*const dplink.Heard = null
    if dpPort(port) { there = &port.*.dp }
    if d.from < ports.*.count && dpPort(from) { before = &from.*.dp }
    mode.makeMove(card, lent.*.readout, lent.*.memory, &target, &monitor, &offer, lent.*.rom, there, before, lent.*.plan)
    mode.say(card, lent.*.plan)
    if lent.*.tables != null {
        const aside = lent.*.tables.?.*.aside
        aside(true)
        mode.list(card, lent.*.plan)
        aside(false)
    }
    var toChannel: ?*aux.Channel = null
    var fromChannel: ?*aux.Channel = null
    if dpPort(port) { toChannel = dpwatch.channelFor(sinks, ports, d.to) }
    if d.from < ports.*.count && dpPort(from) { fromChannel = dpwatch.channelFor(sinks, ports, d.from) }
    _ = changing.heldWith(lent.*.change, lent.*.seen, lent.*.plan, lent.*.result, "the move", toChannel, fromChannel)
    plug.serveAll(card, ports)
    if !carried(card, follow, ports, lent.*.plan, lent.*.result, d) { return false }
    card.say("gpu: the picture goes out by ")
    plug.sayName(card, port)
    card.say(if d.act == Act.move { " now; its memory, size and pitch are as they were: no program is told\n" } else { " again; its memory, size and pitch are as they were\n" })
    return true
}

// What the rule decided at boot, said.
fn sayBoot(card: *const scanout.Card, ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *const Follow, d: Decision) -> void {
    if d.act == Act.none_started {
        card.say("gpu: the firmware started no output of this card, so none of its controllers runs a picture")
        if d.to != NONE {
            card.say(": the monitor on ")
            plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.to])
            card.say(" is not given one")
        }
        card.say(" (a controller started from nothing takes words from one that runs; this driver does not do that)\n")
        return
    }
    if d.act == Act.move {
        card.say("gpu: the monitor is on ")
        plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.to])
        card.say(", the firmware's picture goes out by ")
        plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.from])
        card.say(if ports.*.ports[d.from].level == plug.Level.low { ", where nothing is plugged in" } else { ", where nothing answers" })
        if follow.*.how == How.follows {
            card.say(": the picture is brought to the monitor\n")
        } else {
            card.say(if follow.*.how == How.quiet { ": this boot writes nothing, so the picture stays (a boot of the monitor's own mode would bring it there, if its EDID holds)\n" } else { ": this boot does not set the monitor's mode, so the picture stays (a boot of the monitor's own mode would bring it there)\n" })
        }
        return
    }
    if d.from == NONE { return }
    const showing = &ports.*.ports[d.from]
    card.say("gpu: the picture stays on ")
    plug.sayName(card, showing)
    card.say(if showing.*.level == plug.Level.high { ", where the monitor is\n" } else if showing.*.level == plug.Level.low { ": there is no monitor it can be brought to\n" } else { ": its monitor counts as there\n" })
}

// A connector said once: a second monitor, one that gives no EDID, a
// DisplayPort one, one of another size.
fn sayOther(card: *const scanout.Card, ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *const Follow, d: Decision) -> void {
    const port = &ports.*.ports[d.to]
    if d.act == Act.second {
        card.say("gpu: a second monitor on ")
        plug.sayName(card, port)
        if heard(port) {
            card.size(", ", port.*.monitor.width, port.*.monitor.height)
        }
        card.say(": it is not driven (one picture")
        if d.from != NONE {
            card.say(", on ")
            plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.from])
        }
        card.say(")\n")
    } else if d.act == Act.unanswered {
        card.say("gpu: ")
        plug.sayName(card, port)
        card.say(": something is plugged in and gives no EDID that holds: it is not driven\n")
    } else if d.act == Act.displayport && dpPort(port) {
        card.say("gpu: ")
        plug.sayName(card, port)
        card.say(": its monitor answers on its AUX channel, and no link is trained to it (")
        card.say(dplink.refusalText(port.*.dp.refusal))
        card.say("): it is not driven\n")
    } else if d.act == Act.displayport {
        card.say("gpu: something is plugged into ")
        plug.sayName(card, port)
        card.say(": no path of this driver's leaves by a connector of this kind: it is not driven\n")
    } else if d.act == Act.size {
        card.say("gpu: ")
        plug.sayName(card, port)
        card.size(": the monitor there is ", port.*.monitor.width, port.*.monitor.height)
        card.size(", the picture ", follow.*.width, follow.*.height)
        card.say(": a picture of another size would have to be told to the programs that draw on it, which is not done while brixOS runs; the picture stays where it goes out, and a restart gives the monitor its own mode\n")
    }
}

// C, once: "gpu: connector 2 (HDMI): the monitor has left; nothing else
// has one: the output is kept as it is".
fn sayKept(card: *const scanout.Card, ports: *const plug.Ports, s: usize) -> void {
    card.say("gpu: ")
    plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[s])
    card.say(": the monitor has left and no other connector has one: the output is kept as it is (nothing is taken down)\n")
}

// The showing output's monitor back with the same EDID, or another that
// takes the timing sent already.
fn sayBack(card: *const scanout.Card, ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *const Follow, d: Decision) -> void {
    card.say("gpu: ")
    plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.to])
    card.field(": the monitor is back after ", follow.*.lowFor / 1000000)
    card.say(" ms with its line low")
    // (A DisplayPort output's link was looked at when its monitor came
    // back: gpu_dpwatch.mlx said so, and trained it again if it was lost.)
    const dp = ports.*.ports[d.to].sends == plug.Sends.displayport
    if ports.*.ports[d.to].heard.outcome != ddc.Outcome.read {
        card.say("\n")
    } else if dp {
        card.say("; the output sent all along, its link looked at as the monitor came back (said above): nothing more is written\n")
    } else {
        card.say("; the output sent all along: nothing is written\n")
    }
}

// The monitor back on the DisplayPort output that shows the picture with
// the output not sending (again), or another monitor of the picture's
// size there (other): what is done, in one line.
fn sayDpReturn(card: *const scanout.Card, ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *const Follow, d: Decision) -> void {
    card.say("gpu: ")
    plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.to])
    card.say(if d.act == Act.other { ": another monitor of the picture's size, after " } else { ": the monitor is back after " })
    card.field("", follow.*.lowFor / 1000000)
    card.say(if d.act == Act.other { " ms with the line low: the timing that runs stays, its link looked at as the monitor came (said above); a timing of its own on this DisplayPort output is set at the next start, not while brixOS runs\n" } else { " ms with its line low, and the output does not send: a DisplayPort output's mode is set again at the next start, not while brixOS runs\n" })
}

// What would be done at a boot that follows the monitor.
fn sayWould(card: *const scanout.Card, ports: *const plug.Ports, follow: *const Follow, d: Decision) -> void {
    card.say("gpu: ")
    if d.act == Act.move {
        card.say("the monitor is on ")
        plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.to])
        card.say(" now, and nothing is plugged into ")
        plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.from])
        card.say(": a boot of the monitor's own mode would bring the picture there; this one writes nothing to the display\n")
    } else {
        plug.sayName(card, &ports.*.ports[d.to])
        card.say(": a boot of the monitor's own mode would set its mode again; this one writes nothing to the display\n")
    }
}
